# Tests

Follow `@src/test/java/com/practicetestautomation/tests/login/LoginTests.java` and `@src/test/java/com/practicetestautomation/tests/exceptions/ExceptionsTests.java`. Browser startup and shutdown are `@src/test/java/com/practicetestautomation/tests/BaseTest.java`.

- Put a new area in `src/test/java/com/practicetestautomation/tests/<area>/`. Add login methods to `LoginTests` and exceptions methods to `ExceptionsTests`.
- Extend `BaseTest`. Use its `driver` and `logger`. Do not create a driver, quit it, or set browser options.
- One public `@Test` method per scenario. CamelCase name ending in `Test`.
- Open with `new <Page>(driver)` and `visit()`, then call that object's methods. Assert with `org.testng.Assert`: `assertEquals(actual, expected)` for strings, `assertTrue(condition, "what failed")` for booleans.
- Do not use `By`, waits, or commented-out Selenium in a test.
- Each new method asserts something different. Do not clone `noSuchElementExceptionsTest` and `timeOutExceptionTest`.
- Positive login groups: `positive`, `regression`, `smoke`. Negative login groups: `negative`, `regression`, with `@Parameters({"username","password","expectedErrorMessage"})` filled by the suite. Exceptions methods stay ungrouped unless a suite filters on a group.
- `logger.info` is a single line about the check. Do not create another `Logger`.

## Suites

`mvn test` runs one file under `src/test/resources/TestSuites/`. The default is `FullRegressionSuite.xml`. Match the `<test>`, `<parameter>`, and `<include>` shape of the suite you edit.

- A method runs only when a suite includes it. No `<methods>` block means every `@Test` on that class runs. An `<include name="..."/>` list runs only those methods.
- `SmokeTestSuite.xml` runs the `smoke` group and sets no `browser`.
- Allowed `browser` values are `chrome`, `firefox`, and `edge`.
- A `<test>` that includes `negativeLoginTest` must pass `username`, `password`, and `expectedErrorMessage`.
